@nsobid-4B159F0F7A360669738390EE8657B4F0
// Astral Chain v1.0.1, applied after Dynamic-FPS 1.0.1.pchtxt (native_trace --patch, in that order).
//
// Cutscenes play as in the original game: its own fixed-step timer path (main+0x91DC48, step 1.0 per frame) at a
// steady 30 FPS, while gameplay keeps Dynamic-FPS's measured step at 60 FPS. Measured on the opening cutscene (frames
// from its start to a white flash ~97 s in; the original takes 2910 frames, its audio ~97 s): Dynamic-FPS's step path
// reached it in 2820 frames even at a step of exactly 1.0, i.e. its picture ran ~3 % ahead of the voices at any frame
// rate; at 60 FPS by 2.5-2.8 s at that point. The game's cutscene mode is timer flag bit 30 (w21 == 0 there).
//
// The step code reports cutscene mode to the runtime every frame (svc #0xB1, host_runtime.c.in). In a cutscene the
// runtime sets the step (1.0, plus whole frames when the picture falls a frame or more behind real time after a stall,
// up to 7) and the mod's whole-tick count (+0xD8), and nvn_present_pace (nvn_hle.h) presents at 30 FPS.
// AC_CUTSCENE_FPS=60: cutscenes as gameplay (measured step, 60 FPS).
//
// 0xA0E7F8 held "fmov s1,#2" (the maximum step) in the mod's code cave; it branches to 5 new words after the cave's
// last one (0xA0EFD0), still inside the executable page that ends the text segment.

@flag offset_shift 0x100

@enabled
00A0E7F8 F7010014 // b 0xA0EFD4
00A0EFD4 211600D4 // svc #0xB1: cutscene mode to the runtime; in a cutscene it sets s8 (step) and +0xD8
00A0EFD8 0110201E // fmov s1,#2.0: gameplay maximum step
00A0EFDC 55000035 // cbnz w21,0xA0EFE4: not in a cutscene
00A0EFE0 1A3BFC17 // b 0x91DC48: the original's fixed-step path (str s8,[x19,#0xD0])
00A0EFE4 06FEFF17 // b 0xA0E7FC: fminnm s0,s0,s1
@stop
